From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:26:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] MdeModulePkg/GptLib: Keep the partition entry array
 size in 32 bits

PartitionValidGptTable() checks that NumberOfPartitionEntries *
SizeOfPartitionEntry doesn't overflow MAX_UINTN, but PartitionDxe,
Tcg2 measured boot and GptLib itself compute that product from two
UINT32 fields, in 32 bits. On X64 a header with 0x2000001 entries of
128 bytes passes the check while the product wraps to 128: the entry
array is allocated and CRC-checked at 128 bytes, and the entries are
then read up to 4 GiB past it.

A GPT disk is parsed as soon as it is connected, USB sticks included,
so a crafted one can crash the firmware or leak heap contents.

Bound the product by MAX_UINT32, so every 32-bit computation of it is
exact. Real disks use 128 entries of 128 bytes.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 MdeModulePkg/Library/GptLib/Gpt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Library/GptLib/Gpt.c b/MdeModulePkg/Library/GptLib/Gpt.c
index e83e9806ef..015a0fa146 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/GptLib/Gpt.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/GptLib/Gpt.c
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@ PartitionValidGptTable (
   // are later used to read and size the partition entry array.
   //
   if ((PartHdr->PartitionEntryLBA > DivU64x32 (MAX_UINT64, BlockSize)) ||
-      (PartHdr->NumberOfPartitionEntries > DivU64x32 (MAX_UINTN, PartHdr->SizeOfPartitionEntry)))
+      (PartHdr->NumberOfPartitionEntries > DivU64x32 (MAX_UINT32, PartHdr->SizeOfPartitionEntry)))
   {
     FreePool (PartHdr);
     return FALSE;
